            <ArticleTitle>Existence of cord compression in extramedullary hematopoiesis due to beta thalassemia intermedia.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>183-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1179/102453308X343347</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Extramedullary hematopoiesis (EMH) is a rare disorder, characterized by the appearance of hematopoietic elements outside of the bone marrow, which occurs in patients with chronic myeloproliferative disorders or congenital hemolytic anemias. We report a case with thalassemia intermedia, EMH in spinal cord and a paravertebral mass. We report the case of a 20 year old female who initially presented with back pain and leg weakness was found to have paravertebral mass in the spinal cord.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
